the characters that interfere
  ok   an apostrophe becomes the separator
  ok   a dot does
  ok   a comma does
  ok   a double quote does, and so does a space
  ok   a backslash does
  ok   the separator is configurable: an underscore where that is wanted
  ok   letters, digits, hyphen and underscore are left alone

one character in, one character out
  ok   the length never changes while typing, so the caret never moves
  ok   runs are left alone on the way in
  ok   and collapsed on the way out
  ok   where the ends are trimmed as well
  ok   a trailing separator survives typing -- trimming it makes a two-word name untypeable

the lists, as shipped
  ok   the account list is the rails one
  ok   so is the repository list
  ok   and the view list
  ok   comments are not terms
  ok   the length limit is the rails column's, read from the file
  ok   a reserved account name is refused
  ok   whatever its case
  ok   and a view may not be called `query', which already means something there
  ok   the lists are per kind: what a repository may not be called, a view may
  ok   a longer name that merely begins with a reserved one is not reserved

names that will not be accepted
  ok   an empty name says so
  ok   and so does one with nothing in it but punctuation
  ok   a name past the column's width is refused before the server sees it
  ok   and one that fits is not
  ok   an offensive name is refused
  ok   including an inflection of a listed term, by its segment
  ok   while an ordinary word that merely contains one is not refused
  ok   an acceptable name comes back in the form it will be stored under

without its configuration
  ok   a list that cannot be read is an empty list, not a broken field
  ok   and the sanitising needs no configuration
  ok   nor does the length check

malformed configuration
  ok   a limits file that will not parse leaves the defaults standing
  ok   and the lists it names are still read

